flfiles -- the FreeLFS file manager
===================================

    flfiles [FOLDER]

Window: back, forward, up, an editable path field and a new-folder button on
top; Places (Home and the folders named in ~/.config/user-dirs.dirs, Trash)
and Drives (System = /sysflfs, everything mounted under /drives) on the left;
an icon grid; a status bar. The folder is watched with inotify, so changes
show up on their own. There is no polling: idle means no wakeups.

Hidden files: names with a leading dot, and names listed one per line in the
folder's own .hidden file. Ctrl-H shows them.

Keys: Enter opens, Backspace or Alt-Up goes up, Alt-Left/Right history,
Ctrl-L the path field, F2 rename, Del moves to ~/.local/share/Trash (in the
Trash it deletes for good, after asking), Ctrl-C / Ctrl-X / Ctrl-V copy, cut
and paste (also between two flfiles windows), Ctrl-Shift-N new folder,
Ctrl-A select all, F5 refresh, letters jump to a name. Right click opens a
menu. Ctrl-click and Shift-click select several.

Delete and Move to Trash first ask `flcrash --cant` about the selection: a vital system folder
(/sysflfs, /boot, ...) brings up the "You can't do that." screen, and "Never mind" leaves everything alone.

Enter on a file starts the default app for its MIME type: the type comes from the shared MIME
database (/usr/share/mime/globs2), the app from mimeapps.list ([Default Applications], then
[Added Associations]; ~/.config/mimeapps.list wins over /etc/xdg and the shipped defaults in
/usr/share/applications/mimeapps.list: images -> Images, PDF/EPUB -> Documents, audio -> Music, video ->
Videos, text -> fledit, archives -> Archives), else the first .desktop file that lists the type.
Text files with no known name still open in fledit; a file with no app reports that.
Copying runs in the window's own loop, so a very large copy holds the window.
